[{:db/id "q-112562/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "05fc0b25-f74c-5d87-a779-d8b41c5534d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112562/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "eabc0142-7eb0-5ab1-a6eb-326228eab211" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112562/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "2204fa56-bedf-5d47-b318-62452e053e93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112562/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "5e307926-f7a3-5437-926b-44454610bbb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112562/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "c518d676-877a-5964-8421-6f3a90f5c6e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112562/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "da0e2c83-9ad7-5d96-b0eb-34a56e7f4d98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-112562/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-112562/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-112562/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-112562/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-112562/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-112562/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-112562" :question/id #uuid "98c374fa-24fb-51fc-a983-bcd8e729a379" :question/math-academy-id "q-112562" :question/problem "Let $(x,y)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $x+y?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+3y=15 \\\\ 0.6x-0.8y=1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the second equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+3y=15 &  \\\\ 0.6x-0.8y=1 & |\\,\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}4x+3y=15 \\\\ 6x-8y=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we multiply the first equation by $3$ and the second equation by $-2,$ we will get a $12x$ term in the first equation that can cancel with the $-12x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+3y=15 & |\\,\\times 3 \\\\ 6x-8y=10 & |\\,\\times -2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}12x+9y=45 \\\\ -12x+16y=-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $x$-variable and allows us to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{12x}+9y & =45 \\\\ -\\cancel{12x}+16y & =-20 \\\\ (9y+16y) & =(45-20) \\\\ 25y & =25 \\\\ y & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $y=1$ into the equation $4x+3y=15$ to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y & =15 \\\\ 4x+3 & =15 \\\\ 4x & =15-3 \\\\ 4x & =12 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=3$ and $y=1.$ So, \n\n$$\nx+y=3+1=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-112562/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7578c48-cc9e-5170-8ffe-5ebee6580677"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112562"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-18688/selection/93efa605efcbb4f3458a6b80f318e01ed9a5d70d47b40b7b6bf3758a6ef6ceae" :answer/id #uuid "be36a7c0-12c8-5acd-8f3f-1bb2aeacacb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=1.2,\\,b=1.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18688/selection/ef41f5f3a887733e3ca15cf4bc77a7331fed84deebbdc8b3f25f9fa172781fd7" :answer/id #uuid "f7d33353-f1b6-5902-b2a5-3199f6f564a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=-1.2,\\,b=0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18688/selection/fcc256f374a4c05c09849f374a6b6c957761f5fb403cdef33c9daf3a383a81b4" :answer/id #uuid "517f2e68-a29f-5543-bc82-64db583b6526" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=0.2,\\,b=1.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18688/selection/1ad7b5f946995a5583e27dcffcb1fba8716588acc9adae21e27a50e81b7bce79" :answer/id #uuid "0a565977-2287-518b-8c2d-94568532dbf4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=0.5,\\,b=-1.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18688/selection/88fbb802d70e2d10b38c4035cc72fb6774967799f75030f2b66f754c765b09aa" :answer/id #uuid "175c6f1a-479f-5dde-9299-74ec7dfd10e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=1.5,\\,b=2.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18688/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "17e32d48-05f2-5c8b-b27d-682fc71fd79c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-18688/selection/93efa605efcbb4f3458a6b80f318e01ed9a5d70d47b40b7b6bf3758a6ef6ceae" :answer-field/choices ["q-18688/selection/93efa605efcbb4f3458a6b80f318e01ed9a5d70d47b40b7b6bf3758a6ef6ceae" "q-18688/selection/ef41f5f3a887733e3ca15cf4bc77a7331fed84deebbdc8b3f25f9fa172781fd7" "q-18688/selection/fcc256f374a4c05c09849f374a6b6c957761f5fb403cdef33c9daf3a383a81b4" "q-18688/selection/1ad7b5f946995a5583e27dcffcb1fba8716588acc9adae21e27a50e81b7bce79" "q-18688/selection/88fbb802d70e2d10b38c4035cc72fb6774967799f75030f2b66f754c765b09aa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-18688" :question/id #uuid "8748ba37-2d9a-5451-b497-621aa22378b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-18688" :question/problem "Find the solution of the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}b=2a-1 \\\\ 1.5a+0.5b=2.5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the second equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}b=2a-1 &  \\\\ 1.5a+0.5b=2.5 & |\\,\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}b=2a-1 \\\\ 15a+5b=25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the first equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=2a-1\n$$\n\nNow, to find the value of $a,$ we can substitute $b=2a-1$ into the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15a+5(2a-1) & =25 \\\\ 15a+10a-5 & =25 \\\\ 25a & =30 \\\\ a & =\\frac{30}{25} \\\\ a & =1.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $a=1.2$ into the  first equation to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =2(1.2)-1 \\\\  & =2.4-1 \\\\  & =1.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $a=1.2$ and $b=1.4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-18688/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7578c48-cc9e-5170-8ffe-5ebee6580677"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-18688"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-18827/selection/2cc44a2ad37d484350c370788ff3a46ad029eeea9ffac3ed72ef33c2fd9141f3" :answer/id #uuid "82eb724a-0359-51da-a10b-3d63bb256e18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=0.5,\\,b=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18827/selection/fb5266369b5f49ebc8d33c5ef439a33eff239e7136eb9232207d3a0c6b0a8f6d" :answer/id #uuid "67617072-84e3-53c7-96a3-035c1bf54f6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18827/selection/d4e0b404c90b68a7b4e8873e551e0da7db4ae7dc11cb2a885ea496e646a701c6" :answer/id #uuid "24bca577-e126-5638-9da3-2ed680242cd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18827/selection/2d843451f6f3a857cf24ee9156c2476219b9dc0aa38635965e8ab1f229878090" :answer/id #uuid "c2832ded-941c-51ca-ba7d-742114b4c176" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18827/selection/6b50c86bed78986f139677733b757be9377dcfbb438c8261984cc4ccf02d4b89" :answer/id #uuid "8306b4ac-e73a-5f0c-b5fa-0dafef23d730" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=-0.5,\\,b=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18827/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "50bfc997-fa11-5146-ae99-59a1bd6981aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-18827/selection/6b50c86bed78986f139677733b757be9377dcfbb438c8261984cc4ccf02d4b89" :answer-field/choices ["q-18827/selection/2cc44a2ad37d484350c370788ff3a46ad029eeea9ffac3ed72ef33c2fd9141f3" "q-18827/selection/fb5266369b5f49ebc8d33c5ef439a33eff239e7136eb9232207d3a0c6b0a8f6d" "q-18827/selection/d4e0b404c90b68a7b4e8873e551e0da7db4ae7dc11cb2a885ea496e646a701c6" "q-18827/selection/2d843451f6f3a857cf24ee9156c2476219b9dc0aa38635965e8ab1f229878090" "q-18827/selection/6b50c86bed78986f139677733b757be9377dcfbb438c8261984cc4ccf02d4b89"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-18827" :question/id #uuid "ec708ad2-0528-5c6b-a4f1-9dab6fa5292e" :question/math-academy-id "q-18827" :question/problem "Find the solution of the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}12.8a+6.4=-6.4b \\\\ 2a+1=b\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the first equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}12.8a+6.4=-6.4b & |\\,\\times 10 \\\\ 2a+1=b & \\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}128a+64=-64b \\\\ 2a+1=b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the second equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=2a+1\n$$\n\nNow, to find the value of $a,$ we can substitute $b=2a+1$ into the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}128a+64 & =-64b \\\\ 128a+64 & =-64(2a+1) \\\\ 128a+64 & =-128a-64 \\\\ 256a & =-128 \\\\ a & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ a & =-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $a=-0.5$ into the second equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+1 & =b \\\\ 2(-0.5)+1 & =b \\\\ -1+1 & =b \\\\ b & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-0.5$ and $b=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-18827/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7578c48-cc9e-5170-8ffe-5ebee6580677"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-18827"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-112561/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "2bb080ff-07ac-5d16-acdd-b55afe508236" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112561/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "50fba200-cc50-59ff-8e9d-08ef5d1a4c5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112561/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "cf3d11c1-9f99-5daf-8b7c-e595c728786f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112561/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "cc2d7656-46cf-54bb-95e6-7bb2fa44ef8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112561/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "9bd2c871-f376-54ed-a302-50068a27509b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112561/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "feb69340-ddff-558d-8d5a-1d96eaac1c2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-112561/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-112561/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-112561/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-112561/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-112561/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-112561/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-112561" :question/id #uuid "57dc1d54-5a8e-5211-85bd-cc10abc48676" :question/math-academy-id "q-112561" :question/problem "Let $(x,y)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $x+y?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=7 \\\\ 0.5x+0.4y=0.2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the second equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=7 &  \\\\ 0.5x+0.4y=0.2 & |\\,\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=7 \\\\ 5x+4y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we multiply the  first equation by $-5,$ then we will get a $-5x$ term that can cancel with the $5x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=7 & |\\,\\times (-5) \\\\ 5x+4y=2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}-5x-15y=-35 \\\\ 5x+4y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $x$-variable and allows us to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-\\cancel{5x}-15y & =-35 \\\\ \\cancel{5x}+4y & =2 \\\\ (-15y+4y) & =(-33) \\\\ -11y & =-33 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $y=3$ into the equation $x+3y=7$ to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}x+3y & =7 \\\\ x+3(3) & =7 \\\\ x+9 & =7 \\\\ x & =-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-2,\\,y=3.$ So,\n\n$$\nx+y=(-2)+(3)=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-112561/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7578c48-cc9e-5170-8ffe-5ebee6580677"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112561"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-18702/selection/c59421689e9802bbe55dc885ef3b88a565922fc724e5a7225b403918fe48989b" :answer/id #uuid "1a1dd514-544a-55c9-a2aa-99e818b740ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18702/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "ca0e3238-5f47-505a-b6b2-ec1b087aa0d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18702/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "81751c11-386c-55d9-8ddc-79036db151c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18702/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer/id #uuid "88ec735e-c235-5bae-b747-ecf2b7c29ecd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18702/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "043eba32-079f-5541-bf70-5feec0fae366" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18702/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cddf50a8-a4b3-542e-bb60-d38d89bb54b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-18702/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer-field/choices ["q-18702/selection/c59421689e9802bbe55dc885ef3b88a565922fc724e5a7225b403918fe48989b" "q-18702/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-18702/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-18702/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" "q-18702/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-18702" :question/id #uuid "f271da85-4c2f-5548-b34e-bfcbc915419e" :question/math-academy-id "q-18702" :question/problem "Let $(x,y)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $x-y?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2.3x+4.6y=69 \\\\ 10x-20y=100\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the top equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2.3x+4.6y=69 & |\\,\\times 10 \\\\ 10x-20y=100 & \\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}23x+46y=690 \\\\ 10x-20y=100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we divide the first equation by $23$ and the second equation by $10,$ we will get a $2y$ term in the first equation that can cancel with the $-2y$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}23x+46y=690 & |\\,÷23 \\\\ 10x-20y=100 & |\\,÷10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=30 \\\\ x-2y=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $y$-variable and allows us to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\cancel{2y} & =30 \\\\ x-\\cancel{2y} & =10 \\\\ (x+x) & =(30+10) \\\\ 2x & =40 \\\\ x & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $x=20$ into the equation $x+2y=30$ to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y & =30 \\\\ (20)+2y & =30 \\\\ 2y & =30-20 \\\\ 2y & =10 \\\\ y & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=20$ and $y=5.$ So, \n\n$$\nx-y=20-(5)=15.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-18702/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7578c48-cc9e-5170-8ffe-5ebee6580677"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-18702"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-26223/selection/ad32e20882d861280d8706619fa67dcaa9f21436eff6d7ed2d21b2748b273498" :answer/id #uuid "9772418c-1188-5457-bb21-5aa43d1014fa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=\\frac{5}{3},$ $y=-1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26223/selection/2a7f9a89fd909f7e7c9c5ea8e087c679cc123dda00ce3286eda011196f13dd9e" :answer/id #uuid "06c74088-0ffe-53af-898c-82f752b76c78" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=1,$ $y=-3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26223/selection/821fde864f550c94c476be392e4fb0d6c00219bd377eb5bddbd9e824279b6f7f" :answer/id #uuid "f2a3a49f-dfa9-5c2c-9f37-0bc9132a8eb0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=\\frac{7}{3},$ $y=1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26223/selection/114072da1c183c2b839016822cd01bd3b4bb6ced47b2afe79fca0fa2e5d9c6dc" :answer/id #uuid "6dde04b4-25e8-55ed-afe9-fda0403c4729" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=\\frac{4}{3},$ $y=-2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26223/selection/87ce5f8f6550b52371ecd6d6b7d95627d50c242d6774859c4b97279942afbf38" :answer/id #uuid "4a07a067-9855-5e91-93a1-f1bc495b21db" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2,$ $y=0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26223/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "10936f57-bd98-5481-94b8-cd4228f57c8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-26223/selection/ad32e20882d861280d8706619fa67dcaa9f21436eff6d7ed2d21b2748b273498" :answer-field/choices ["q-26223/selection/ad32e20882d861280d8706619fa67dcaa9f21436eff6d7ed2d21b2748b273498" "q-26223/selection/2a7f9a89fd909f7e7c9c5ea8e087c679cc123dda00ce3286eda011196f13dd9e" "q-26223/selection/821fde864f550c94c476be392e4fb0d6c00219bd377eb5bddbd9e824279b6f7f" "q-26223/selection/114072da1c183c2b839016822cd01bd3b4bb6ced47b2afe79fca0fa2e5d9c6dc" "q-26223/selection/87ce5f8f6550b52371ecd6d6b7d95627d50c242d6774859c4b97279942afbf38"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-26223" :question/id #uuid "3d7c59ff-df86-5863-a05a-c20fb84b2ead" :question/math-academy-id "q-26223" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.3x-0.1y=0.6 \\\\ 0.6x+0.8y=0.2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply both equations by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.3x-0.1y=0.6 & |\\,\\times 10 \\\\ 0.6x+0.8y=0.2 & |\\,\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}3x-y=6 \\\\ 6x+8y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we divide the second equation by $(-2),$ we will get a $-3x$ term in the second equation that can cancel with the $3x$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-y=6 &  \\\\ 6x+8y=2 & |\\,÷(-2)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}3x-y=6 \\\\ -3x-4y=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $x$-variable and allows us to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{3x}-y & =6 \\\\ -\\cancel{3x}-4y & =-1 \\\\ (-y-4y) & =(6-1) \\\\ -5y & =5 \\\\ y & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $y=-1$ into the equation $3x-y=6$ to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-y & =6 \\\\ 3x-(-1) & =6 \\\\ 3x & =5 \\\\ x & =\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=\\frac{5}{3}$ and $y=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-26223/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc62d8df-450f-5f7a-b647-b53c051f8339"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-26223"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-18831/selection/050da5b1df27941d7398c3ca88f050f09c7e33dff1555f94c7e01179e1371ebf" :answer/id #uuid "4bea154a-0961-5d9f-8b44-5d5366c31f6a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$v=-75,$ $w=-170$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18831/selection/3cb90c821f97ff9a26c83de51363d997f7364afb24528865285f52382841f363" :answer/id #uuid "ee3cfdfa-0bad-5ac9-8f20-e6c0cc73406e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$v=0,$ $w=-20$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18831/selection/976acf621a9dd5c1ec74134c60236c069e44ebee9a227a27f6da3fabc697960b" :answer/id #uuid "54582aaf-16c4-5547-9138-a7fe1bb1a4b5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$v=50,$ $w=80$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18831/selection/eca3407cc801d82d90b222fd4d588e823d80da6dbfcbc4c5153580195c77ec0a" :answer/id #uuid "446ebbac-38c1-54e0-b482-d681af127503" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$v=-50,$ $w=-120$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18831/selection/f296f59f648e2267ab08d509a743b536fbffdc01e1dcfd6a6aab3b792037f812" :answer/id #uuid "b538716a-5edf-5471-8c28-95a00972207a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$v=25,$ $w=30$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18831/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6192324-5003-5119-9a67-ea2ffe996700" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-18831/selection/050da5b1df27941d7398c3ca88f050f09c7e33dff1555f94c7e01179e1371ebf" :answer-field/choices ["q-18831/selection/050da5b1df27941d7398c3ca88f050f09c7e33dff1555f94c7e01179e1371ebf" "q-18831/selection/3cb90c821f97ff9a26c83de51363d997f7364afb24528865285f52382841f363" "q-18831/selection/976acf621a9dd5c1ec74134c60236c069e44ebee9a227a27f6da3fabc697960b" "q-18831/selection/eca3407cc801d82d90b222fd4d588e823d80da6dbfcbc4c5153580195c77ec0a" "q-18831/selection/f296f59f648e2267ab08d509a743b536fbffdc01e1dcfd6a6aab3b792037f812"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-18831" :question/id #uuid "3af04ac3-aff2-5a62-a4f3-e410d24890bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-18831" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.09v-0.04w=0.05 \\\\ 0.02v-0.01w=0.2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply both equations by $100,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.09v-0.04w=0.05 & |\\times 100 \\\\ 0.02v-0.01w=0.2 & |\\times 100\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}9v-4w=5 \\\\ 2v-w=20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we multiply the second equation by $-4,$ we will get a $4w$ term that can cancel with the $-4w$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}9v-4w=5 &  \\\\ 2v-w=20 & |\\,\\times (-4)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}9v-4w=5 \\\\ -8v+4w=-80\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $w$-variable and allows us to solve for $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9v-\\cancel{4w} & =5 \\\\ -8v+\\cancel{4w} & =-80 \\\\ (9v-8v) & =(5-80) \\\\ v & =-75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $v=-75$ into the equation $2v-w=20$ to solve for $w:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2v-w & =20 \\\\ 2(-75)-w & =20 \\\\ -150-w & =20 \\\\ -w & =170 \\\\ w & =-170\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $v=-75,\\,w=-170.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-18831/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc62d8df-450f-5f7a-b647-b53c051f8339"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-18831"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-18720/selection/a39e4c3855e119cc134cd501616b2d4242dd33fe6134da1d7da0776d673411f7" :answer/id #uuid "95337147-3f23-562d-b3c0-f508168a3c6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18720/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "afde4537-0447-5bd5-9358-fce72150f84b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18720/selection/4f47ddc6635e43a7d9f63a5c4e57d8aff58b02baa07376daf893caae466b70e3" :answer/id #uuid "435e1f44-ee49-53a1-949b-55d256fc75d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18720/selection/ab3343a580c9ecbbb4e27d0c43b67b7d3815a6806a811b62927c9243c7c87034" :answer/id #uuid "12e38895-bd61-59cb-bc21-38804f861111" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18720/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "526622a4-637e-525a-b1ba-68a009ebc175" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18720/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8962d05-7e6a-5a7e-926b-dabbe183c86e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-18720/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-18720/selection/a39e4c3855e119cc134cd501616b2d4242dd33fe6134da1d7da0776d673411f7" "q-18720/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-18720/selection/4f47ddc6635e43a7d9f63a5c4e57d8aff58b02baa07376daf893caae466b70e3" "q-18720/selection/ab3343a580c9ecbbb4e27d0c43b67b7d3815a6806a811b62927c9243c7c87034" "q-18720/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-18720" :question/id #uuid "b71e530d-e775-501c-9fa4-f49030e390f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-18720" :question/problem "Let $(p,q)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $p+2q?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.36p+1.2q=0.36 \\\\ -1.9p-7.6q=3.8\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the first equation by $100$ and the second equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.36p+1.2q=0.36 & |\\times 100 \\\\ -1.9p-7.6q=3.8 & |\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}36p+120q=36 \\\\ -19p-76q=38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can solve for $p$ in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-19p-76q & =38 \\\\ -19p & =76q+38 \\\\ p & =\\frac{76q+38}{-19} \\\\ p & =-4q-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the value of $q,$ we can substitute $p=-4q-2$ into the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}36p+120q & =36 \\\\ 36(-4q-2)+120q & =36 \\\\ -144q-72+120q & =36 \\\\ -24q & =108 \\\\ q & =-\\frac{108}{24} \\\\ q & =-4.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $q=-4.5$ into the equation $p=-4q-2$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =-4q-2 \\\\ p & =-4(-4.5)-2 \\\\ p & =18-2 \\\\ p & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=16$ and $q=-4.5.$ So, \n\n$$\np+2q=16+2(-4.5)=16-9=7.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-18720/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc62d8df-450f-5f7a-b647-b53c