ate]} {:db/id "q-112564" :question/id #uuid "c910bf18-c47e-55bc-8cc2-bd689ff5d040" :question/math-academy-id "q-112564" :question/problem "Let $(a,b)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $a+b?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}a+1.5b-6=0 \\\\ 0.6a-0.4b-1=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply both equations by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}a+1.5b-6=0 & |\\,\\times 10 \\\\ 0.6a-0.4b-1=0 & |\\,\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}10a+15b-60=0 \\\\ 6a-4b-10=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we  multiply the first equation by $\\frac{2}{5}$ and the second equation by $\\frac{3}{2},$ we will get a $6b$ term in the first equation that can cancel with the $-6b$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}10a+15b-60=0 & |\\,\\times \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 6a-4b-10=0 & |\\,\\times \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}4a+6b-24=0 \\\\ 9a-6b-15=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $b$-variable and allows us to solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a+\\cancel{6b}-24 & =0 \\\\ 9a-\\cancel{6b}-15 & =0 \\\\ (4a+9a)+(-24-15) & =0 \\\\ 13a-39 & =0 \\\\ a & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $a=3$ into the equation $6a-4b-10=0$ to solve for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6a-4b-10 & =0 \\\\ 6(3)-4b-10 & =0 \\\\ 18-4b-10 & =0 \\\\ 8-4b & =0 \\\\ b & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $a=3$ and $b=2.$ So, \n\n$$\na+b=3+2=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-112564/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc62d8df-450f-5f7a-b647-b53c051f8339"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112564"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-18853/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "3cc72e39-e5d9-5c68-b1d0-8aa36d554cc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18853/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "0158c616-cb2f-5e32-af59-5b48a43c9810" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18853/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "6a88a648-90b2-5754-9b51-efb0ab983224" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18853/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer/id #uuid "8635826a-9330-5f5c-989a-b191eac68ff6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18853/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "487e7e86-c64d-5013-9120-349863e41031" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18853/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "30c70cfc-4394-59f8-a13e-057991ac0dfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-18853/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-18853/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-18853/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-18853/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-18853/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" "q-18853/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-18853" :question/id #uuid "c87ad3c5-91fd-58f1-b98c-7515580415bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-18853" :question/problem "Let $(v,w)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $v+w?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.5v-2.5w=7.5 \\\\ 0.7v+0.3w=2.9\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply both equations by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.5v-2.5w=7.5 & |\\times 10 \\\\ 0.7v+0.3w=2.9 & |\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}5v-25w=75 \\\\ 7v+3w=29\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can solve for $v$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5v-25w & =75 \\\\ 5v & =25w+75 \\\\ v & =\\frac{25w+75}{5} \\\\ v & =5w+15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the value of $w,$ we can substitute $v=5w+15$ into the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7v+3w & =29 \\\\ 7(5w+15)+3w & =29 \\\\ 35w+105+3w & =29 \\\\ 38w & =-76 \\\\ w & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $w=-2$ into the equation $v=5w+15$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =5w+15 \\\\ v & =5(-2)+15 \\\\ v & =-10+15 \\\\ v & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $v=5,\\,w=-2.$ So,\n\n$$\nv+w=5+(-2)=3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-18853/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc62d8df-450f-5f7a-b647-b53c051f8339"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-18853"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
